@@ -0,0 +1,142 @@
+# AutoDebug: LLM smoke runtime loses the external port and runtime controls
+
+## Scope and direct evidence
+
+This inspection-only pass examined the latest smoke log,
+`run_2026-08-12_22-29-24_id_autoport-Falcon3-7B-Base_p300x2_benchmarks_2cD4WPKa.log`,
+and the current TTI source. No implementation code was edited.
+
+The log proves the previous parser layers are cleared:
+
+- runtime identity is `Falcon3-7B-Base`, autoport implementation, `p300x2`;
+- `service_port=8000` and `disable_trace_capture=True` are present;
+- the workflow reaches the LLM benchmark and expands eight sweep points;
+- execution blocks in `RemoteOpenAIController.wait_for_healthy()` until it is
+  interrupted.
+
+The corresponding combined spec has one performance-reference target
+(`isl=8`, `osl=8`, concurrency 1, one prompt), `limit_samples_mode=None`, and
+`disable_trace_capture=True`.
+
+## Finding 1: remote URL construction drops a separately supplied service port
+
+The initial report wording is slightly stale: current
+`llm_performance_tests.py:63-80` does not pass `ctx.server_url` directly to the
+controller. It creates:
+
+1. `server_base_url = ctx.server_url` for a remote run;
+2. `ServerConnection(base_url=server_base_url, service_port=ctx.server_port,
+   is_remote=True)`;
+3. `RemoteOpenAIController(base_url=server.url_with_port)`.
+
+However, `ServerConnection.url_with_port` returns the bare `base_url` whenever
+`is_remote` is true (`llm_module/config.py:69-77`). Because the smoke supplied
+`--server-url http://127.0.0.1` separately from `--service-port 8000`, the
+result remains `http://127.0.0.1`, not `http://127.0.0.1:8000`.
+`RemoteOpenAIController.models_url` consequently becomes
+`http://127.0.0.1/v1/models` (`llm_module/server_control.py:127-147`). This
+fully predicts a readiness wait while the verified endpoint at port 8000 is
+healthy.
+
+The same `ServerConnection` is passed to the benchmark driver, so this is not
+only a readiness-probe concern: a remote driver that consumes
+`server.url_with_port` can also target the wrong port after readiness is fixed.
+
+### Fix boundary
+
+Use the already canonical `MediaContext.base_url`, which calls
+`build_base_url(_deploy_url, service_port)` and preserves an explicit URL port
+while otherwise appending the separate service port
+(`test_module/context.py:49-69`). Construct the remote `ServerConnection` and
+controller from that canonical URL, or change `ServerConnection.url_with_port`
+so `is_remote` does not suppress a missing service port. The former is the
+narrower caller-boundary fix; the latter needs broader driver regression tests.
+
+Do not hard-code 8000. Tests must cover a host-only URL plus non-default port,
+an explicitly ported URL whose port wins, and local split host/port behavior.
+
+## Finding 2: `disable_trace_capture` reaches the context but is not passed to the runner
+
+The combined runtime config carries `disable_trace_capture=True`, and
+`CommandFactory._build_context()` places that `RuntimeConfig` on
+`MediaContext`. `LLMPerformanceRunner.run()` exposes the relevant contract as
+`skip_trace_capture=False`; it calls `capture_traces()` when false and sweep
+shapes exist (`llm_module/runner.py:72-101`).
+
+`run_llm_performance()` currently calls
+`runner.run(configs, server, context)` without the keyword
+(`test_module/llm_tests/llm_performance_tests.py:88-92`). Therefore the runtime
+flag is semantically dropped.
+
+The live remote controller's `capture_traces()` is presently a no-op, so this
+omission did not cause the readiness hang. It is still a real contract bug: it
+will enable capture for another controller or after remote capture gains an
+implementation, contrary to the requested release spec.
+
+### Fix boundary
+
+Derive `skip_trace_capture` from
+`ctx.runtime_config.disable_trace_capture` (false when no runtime config) in
+`run_llm_performance()` and pass it explicitly to `runner.run()`. A focused
+mock-runner test should prove true and false propagation independently of the
+controller's current no-op behavior.
+
+## Finding 3: eight points are expected when neither smoke selection nor target-only mode is active
+
+`run_llm_bench()` obtains `limit_samples_mode` from the runtime config and calls
+`get_llm_configs()` (`test_module/llm_tests/llm_benchmark_tests.py:97-106`).
+The smoke's runtime value is `None`, so `get_llm_configs()` does not call
+`select_smoke_test_benchmark_config()`.
+
+`build_benchmark_config()` always starts with the model's performance-reference
+task, then appends generated benchmark sweep tasks unless the environment
+variable `ONLY_BENCHMARK_TARGETS` is non-empty
+(`reference_config/benchmarking/benchmark_config.py:614-617`). The model has
+one target, but the generated valid text shapes/concurrencies expand the final
+deduplicated list to the eight points logged. The count is therefore selection
+behavior, not evidence that the custom spec was ignored.
+
+### Supported one-target controls
+
+- Preferred CLI/runtime smoke control: pass outer
+  `--limit-samples-mode smoke-test`. It is serialized into the combined
+  `RuntimeConfig`; `get_llm_configs()` then selects only the first task, which
+  is the one-entry performance-reference task for this spec.
+- Narrow environment control: `ONLY_BENCHMARK_TARGETS=1` suppresses generated
+  sweeps and retains performance targets. This is appropriate for a targeted
+  harness invocation, but note that the implementation treats *any* non-empty
+  value, including `"0"`, as enabled.
+
+Neither control should become a release default. The tiny pre-release smoke
+may select one target; nightly/full release must retain its intended sweep.
+
+## Focused experiments
+
+1. Build a remote `MediaContext(server_url="http://127.0.0.1",
+   service_port=8123)` and spy on `RemoteOpenAIController`; assert readiness and
+   driver connection both use `http://127.0.0.1:8123`.
+2. Repeat with `server_url="http://127.0.0.1:9000"`; assert 9000 wins over the
+   separate service port and is not duplicated.
+3. Mock `LLMPerformanceRunner.run`; assert runtime
+   `disable_trace_capture=True/False` maps to
+   `skip_trace_capture=True/False`.
+4. Use the Falcon custom spec with no selection control and assert the current
+   eight configs, showing that the runtime spec is honored but sweeps append.
+5. Set `limit_samples_mode="smoke-test"`; assert exactly its one performance
+   target remains. Independently set `ONLY_BENCHMARK_TARGETS=1` and assert the
+   same one target for this spec.
+6. After fixes, rerun only the tiny client smoke against the existing server;
+   verify `/v1/models` polling includes port 8000, trace capture is skipped,
+   and exactly one benchmark command starts.
+
+## Self-review and remaining uncertainty
+
+The port-loss and trace-flag findings are source-proven, and the observed hang
+and eight-point count match their predictions. The claim that the controller
+was directly constructed from `ctx.server_url` was corrected after inspecting
+current source: the loss occurs one layer later in
+`ServerConnection.url_with_port` because `is_remote=True`.
+
+No hardware or live request was issued in this pass. After the focused unit
+tests, the existing server smoke remains necessary to prove the complete URL
+and driver path in the workflow virtual environment.
